course: dictionary
lesson: 13926
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word «lefty» is one of them. Read the sentence around it, and the clues will tell you which meaning the writer means. «Mia is a lefty, so she writes with her left hand.» Here the clue is writes with her left hand, so a lefty is a left-handed person.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «The councillor was called a lefty by her rivals, but she just smiled.» Here the clue is that she was called a name in an argument about politics, so lefty means a person with left-wing political views.
explain: Always try your meaning in the sentence. If it makes sense, you have found the right one. If it does not, try the other meaning. Lefty is informal, which means it is a relaxed, everyday word, not a formal one.
fact: «Lefty» is an informal word for a left-handed person.
fact: About 1 in 10 people are left-handed.
fact: In sport, a «lefty» can be a left-handed pitcher in baseball or a left-handed tennis player.
fact: In politics, «lefty» means a person with left-wing political views, and it is sometimes said as a mild insult.
fact: When someone calls you a lefty in a teasing or rude way, the context and the tone of voice tell you how they mean it.
exercise: «Mia is a lefty, so she writes with her left hand.» What is a lefty here? | A person who lives on the left side of the street | *A left-handed person | A player who runs very fast | A pencil case
exercise: «The lefty pitcher threw the ball so fast that the batter missed it.» Which sport is this? | Cooking | Chess | *Baseball | Swimming
exercise: «Some people called the councillor a lefty, but she only shrugged.» What does lefty mean here? | A person who sings quietly | *A person with left-wing political views | A person who is good at tennis | A person who forgets things
test:
«The lefty tennis player served an ace.» What is a lefty here? | A player who wears a left shoe | A player who is always late | *A left-handed player | A player who has lost
test:
Ben's brother said «You're such a lefty!» in a teasing voice. Why might someone say lefty as a mild insult? | Because it means they are very kind | *Because it is used to tease people about their left-wing political views | Because it means they are very tall | Because it is always a compliment
exam:
«Lefty» can mean a left-handed person or a person with left-wing political views. Which is true? | Only a left-handed person | Only a person who plays tennis | *Both are meanings in the dictionary | It is the name of a country
